er. Initially, create a multi-ring buffer for the area.shp file with distances of 100, 200, 300, and 400 meters. Then, overlay the road.shp file with this buffer to conduct spatial analysis. Upon completion, save the analyzed results as a new Shapefile., Data files are stored under WORKING_DIRECTORY/data/.../...', 'manager_repeat_count': 1, 'coder_state': '', 'reporter_state': '', 'cartographer_state': '', 'code_reviewer_state': "CONTINUE: Both required output files are present in the working directory:\n\n- **`coder/subtask_1/disaster_impact_roads.shp`** — the overlay analysis result (roads clipped to each buffer ring)\n- **`coder/subtask_1/multi_ring_buffers.shp`** — the four multi-ring buffer polygons (100m, 200m, 300m, 400m)\n\nThese match the Manager's instructions: multi-ring buffers around `area.shp` were created and spatially overlaid with `road.shp`, and the analyzed results were saved as a new Shapefile. The subtask is complete.", 'map_reviewer_state': '', 'report_reviewer_state': '', 'needs_revision': False, 'revision_count': 0, 'sender': 'manager', 'is_last_step': False}
